{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789900757,"nonce":"KmNT1jLzTe01vQKhzZdatZv5spA=","title":"`Array.remove(x)` removed by INDEX, and never a string by content","message":"The row bound `remove` to `haxe_array_remove(arr, index)`, so `a.remove(obj)` returned false (or removed an unrelated slot when the pointer happened to be a small number): `Xml.addChild` never detached a node from its old parent (TestXML testMore, Issue4094). Now `haxe_array_remove_value` compares bits, as `indexOf` does, and an `Array\u003cString\u003e` receiver goes through the string search the way `indexOf`/`contains` already do. Also: a literal typed by every element as one Haxe type is homogeneous however its elements arrive as registers (`[\"\u003c\", String.fromCharCode(0x3F)]` boxed the literals and left the call result raw). `StringIteratorUnicode`/`StringKeyValueIteratorUnicode` decode UTF-8 on rayzor (`#elseif rayzor`), since `target.unicode` is now defined and `htmlEscape` re-encoded each byte.","files":null}]}